# Manual requests for the running stack (`docker compose up -d`).
# VS Code: install "REST Client" (humao.rest-client), then click "Send Request" above each request.
# Ports come from .env (made by `yarn setup`), so they match whatever ports your machine got.

@api = http://localhost:{{$dotenv LB_HOST_PORT}}
@pos = http://localhost:{{$dotenv FAKE_POS_PORT}}

### 1. Create a check
# @name create
POST {{api}}/checks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "restaurantId": "r1",
  "items": [{ "name": "Koshary", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 45 }],
  "total": 90
}

### 2. Pay it (answers fast; the worker delivers to the POS in the background)
POST {{api}}/checks/{{create.response.body.id}}/pay

### 3. Where is it in the POS sync? (pending → synced within a second or two)
GET {{api}}/checks/{{create.response.body.id}}/sync

### 4. Cancel it (the worker then cancels the POS order)
POST {{api}}/checks/{{create.response.body.id}}/cancel

### 5. What does the POS hold right now?
GET {{pos}}/debug/orders


### ---------- Permanent rejection (422) and manual retry ----------

### 6. A check the POS will reject: total <= 0
# @name rejected
POST {{api}}/checks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "restaurantId": "r1",
  "items": [{ "name": "Free sample", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 0 }],
  "total": 0
}

### 7. Pay it
POST {{api}}/checks/{{rejected.response.body.id}}/pay

### 8. Sync shows status "failed" and the POS's reason in lastError
GET {{api}}/checks/{{rejected.response.body.id}}/sync

### 9. Retry by hand (202). It will fail again: the total is still 0
POST {{api}}/checks/{{rejected.response.body.id}}/sync/retry

### 10. Retry on a sync that isn't stopped → 409
POST {{api}}/checks/{{create.response.body.id}}/sync/retry


### ---------- Utilities ----------

### Health of the API behind the load balancer
GET {{api}}/health

### Empty the fake POS (orders and rate limiter)
POST {{pos}}/debug/reset
